  <exercise data-content-id="85e6ea4a-1b2d-4462-93b2-3e7ee9cbb4b7" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-solution="\(f(x) = (x + 3)(x - 2)\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(f(x) = (x - 3)(x - 2)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(f(x) = (x - 3)(x + 2)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(f(x) = (x + 3)(x - 2)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(f(x) = (x + 3)(x + 2)\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Examine the graph.</para>
      <para><figure><media alt="GRAPH OF A PARABOLA THAT OPENS UPWARD WITH A \(y\)-intercepts OF NEGATIVE 6 AND \(x\)-intercepts OF NEGATIVE 3 AND 2."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/52aee621abcd499b8e72ef1bad0d62b55e8334ce"/></media></figure></para>
      <para>Which function matches the graph?</para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct!</para>
    </solution>
    </exercise>
